  "worked_solution": "We count the number of squares. We see that there are $3$ squares.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $9$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of circles to total shapes is $3:9.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of squares to the total shapes is $1:3.$",
